<title>SOUTH AFRICA: GOLF-LEADING SECOND ROUND SCORES IN SOUTH AFRICAN OPEN.</title>
<headline>GOLF-LEADING SECOND ROUND SCORES IN SOUTH AFRICAN OPEN.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading scores from the</p>
<p>second round of the 3.4 million rand (745,000 dollars) South</p>
<p>African Open at par 72 Glendower golf course on Saturday (South</p>
<p>African unless stated):</p>
<p>135 Wayne Bradley 65 70, Thomas Bjorn (Denmark) 66 69, David</p>
<p>Gilford (Britain) 69 66, Vijay Singh (Fiji) 69 66</p>
<p>136 Eamonn Darcy (Ireland) 67 69</p>
<p>137 Fulton Allem 66 71, Jean van de Velde (France) 68 69</p>
<p>138 Nick Price (Zimbabwe) 72 66, Mark McNulty (Zimbabwe) 69 69,</p>
<p>Ernie Els 66 72</p>
<p>139 Retief Goosen 72 67, Adam Hunter (Britain) 71 68, Philip</p>
<p>Price (Britain) 71 68, Wayne Westner 69 70</p>
<p>140 Kevin Stone 70 70, Clinton Whitelaw 74 66, Bobby Lincoln 71</p>
<p>69, Gary Evans (Britain) 68 72, Justin Hobday 72 68</p>
<p>141 Nico van Rensburg 69 72, Ian Woosnam (Britain) 66 75, Sven</p>
<p>Struver (Germany) 70 71, Sammy Daniels 71 70, Ian Palmer 76 65,</p>
<p>Marco Gortana 74 67, Robert Karlsson (Sweden) 71 70, Fran Quinn</p>
<p>junior (U.S.) 69 72</p>
<p>Selected scores: 142 David Frost 70 72</p>
<p>Missed cut: 148 Wayne Riley (Australia) 72 76, Costatino</p>
<p>Rocca (Italy) 72 76</p>
<p>Note: Play was suspended on Friday with only half the second</p>
<p>round completed due to lightning.</p>
</text>
